  U2 still before release: still_window_max_mm < 1.5 (the RELEASE_AUTO limit; the show holds R-1)
  U3 heading held: no heading vertex moves more than 1 cm from its pinned height after the release
  U4 unrolled in time: hem mean z <= lift + 0.25 x drop by 60 frames (2 s) after the release
  U5 hang: the existing hang_profile at the LAST frame passes (flare <= 1.15; folds kept >= 0.75 and depth >= 0.5 at
     75/50/25% of the height)
  U6 hem clear of the floor (min z >= 2 cm) and stretch (heading - hem) / drop <= 1.03
  U7 settled: largest per-vertex move over the last 30 frames < 2 mm (the frame the show holds after the unroll)
  Plus the eye: the clip (CLIP_STEP=1) from R-30, judged by Gary. Numbers pass a look; they do not approve it.

